~ start
# step 2.294: once julian has given his lead, there's nothing more to talk about.
if Flags.get_level_flag("julian_password_asked") == true:
	Player: (I doubt there's much left for us to discuss with him.)
	=> END
do stage_party("Julian", "base")
# step 2.396: Julian's theme, for as long as he's in the conversation (it fades when he turns away or the
# talk ends)
do SoundManager.play_music_track("julian_hub_theme", 2.0)
# step 2.375: Layla's expressions (rig). around Julian she's polite but unsure of herself; she enters as
# "base" and this lands while she fades in.
do actor_change("Layla", "pensive")
do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
Julian: Yes?
=> hub

~ hub
do actor_change("Layla", "pensive")
do actor_change("Julian", "base")
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
What do you want to say to him?
- What were you talking about on the phone?
	=> phone_talk
- Ask him about the keypad password. [Proceed] [if (Flags.get_level_flag("lab_keypad_interacted") == true and Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_date_hint_given") == true) or Flags.get_level_flag("dev_julian_all_topics") == true]
	=> keypad_password
- Nothing. Never mind. [Leave]
	=> leave

~ phone_talk
do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back")
Player: Saw you talking pretty intensely over the phone.
Player: Didn't seem like a pleasant conversation.
do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
Julian: It wasn't.
Julian: It also doesn't concern you.
do actor_change("Julian", "explain_talk")
Julian: No wonder you all are scrambling over in the Genomics department.
Julian: No one there wants to work anymore.
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	do actor_change("Layla", "angry_talk")
	do actor_change("Julian", "explain")
	Layla: Well, we're at work right now!
	do actor_change("Layla", "angry")
	do actor_change("Julian", "explain_talk")
	Julian: Are you? I thought you were just visiting.
	# step 2.376: troubled from her own "Umm..." line, held through Julian's
	do actor_change("Layla", "troubled")
	do actor_change("Julian", "explain")
	Layla: Umm... yes, I am doing that...
	Layla: But also...
	do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
	Julian: I'd love to know more, but I'm very busy right now.
do actor_change("Julian", "base")
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: Right. Carry on, then.
do actor_change("Julian", "annoyed_talk")
Julian: Anything else you want to waste my time with?
=> hub

~ keypad_password
do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back")
Player: Listen. Seems like someone changed our lab's password yesterday.
Player: Any chance you know the updated one?
do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
Julian: Not really. I barely visit your lab anyway.
do actor_change("Julian", "explain_talk")
Julian: The last one I remember using was the date of independence.
do actor_change("Julian", "explain")
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: Yeah. Unfortunately, that isn't working anymore.
do actor_change("Julian", "explain_talk")
Julian: Too bad. Why don't you call your professor and ask him?
do actor_change("Julian", "base")
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
	do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
	Layla: Well, we... can't do that.
	do actor_change("Layla", "troubled")
Player: Yeah. It's complicated.
do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
Julian: Well, too bad, I guess.
Julian: Anyway, I need to get back to work. So, will there be anything else?
do actor_change("Julian", "base")
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	do actor_change("Layla", "explaining_talk")
	do actor_effect("Layla", "lean_in")
	Layla: Actually... the janitor told us that all his previous passwords have been dates.
	do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
	Layla: Would you, by any chance, be aware of any such dates that the professor would've been fond of?
	do actor_change("Layla", "attentive")
else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	do actor_effect("Layla", "upright")
do actor_change("Julian", "think_talk")
Julian: Hmmm. I'm not su-
do actor_effect("Julian", "shock")
Julian: Wait.
do actor_focus("Julian", 1.5, 0.5, 0.565)
Julian: Come to think of it, he did mention some important event in genomics to me about a week ago, when I went to see him for counsel.
Julian: Something about... Crick, Watson, and some other guy.
Julian: How everyone credits them with discovering DNA, when what they actually figured out was its structure.
do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
Julian: The double helix. I hope you've heard of it.
do actor_focus("Fiona", 1.5, 0.35)
do actor_change("Julian", "base")
do actor_change("Fiona", "suspicious")
Player: (This cheeky bastard.)
do actor_change("Fiona", "shrug")
Player: Oh no! How could I have ever heard of that?
do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
Player: It's not like I'm the youngest lead researcher under the most celebrated genomicist in the world.
do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
Julian: Right. Indeed, you're not. You're just the lead who seems to be locked out of her own lab.
do actor_change("Julian", "base")
do actor_change("Fiona", "shy")
You almost crack a smile. Almost.
Player: (Bastard.)
do actor_focus("Julian", 1.5, 0.35, 0.565)
do actor_change("Julian", "explain_talk")
Julian: Anyway. The molecule itself was found more than eighty years earlier, by some Swiss guy whose name I can't recall.
do actor_unfocus_all(0.4)
Julian: He seemed rather fond of that fact. I remember he rattled off some dates too.
do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
Julian: Well. That's all I can say. I don't remember what those dates were.
do Flags.set_level_flag("julian_password_asked", true)
do actor_change("Julian", "base")
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
	do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
	Layla: Oh my god! This is great!
	do party_huddle()
	do actor_change("Layla", "explaining_talk")
	Layla: Fiona, it's highly likely that one of those dates is the key to the lab!
	Layla: All we need to do is find out what those dates were!
	do actor_change("Layla", "happy_talk")
	Layla: Lemme just quickly google this.
	# step 2.404: her phone, held up beside her until she gives up on it
	do actor_item("Layla", "phone")
	do actor_change("Layla", "neutral")
	She whips out her phone.
	do actor_change("Layla", "whining")
	do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
	Layla: Oh no! My battery's run out.
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_phone_dead_known", true)
	do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
	Layla: Fiona, could we use your phone to...
	do actor_change("Layla", "troubled")
	She stops mid-sentence, remembering your phone situation.
	do actor_item_hide("Layla")
	Player: Well, I guess you already know the answer to that question.
	do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
	Layla: Yeah. I remember you use a dumb phone with no internet.
	do actor_change("Layla", "touched")
	Player: It's great for focus.
	# a doubtful side glance, mouth shut on purpose
	do actor_change("Layla", "smug")
	Layla: Sure...
	do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
	Layla stares at the floor.
	do party_unhuddle()
else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
# step 2.375: she looks up hopefully, then tenses at his question (same pose)
do actor_change("Layla", "pensive")
do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back")
Player: Anyway, do you think you could search for those dates quickly on your phone?
do actor_change("Julian", "sus")
Julian: ...
do actor_effect("Julian", "lean_in")
do actor_change("Layla", "surprised")
do actor_change("Julian", "sus_talk")
Julian: Perhaps. First, tell me. Why can't you really ask your professor?
- That's none of your business. [matters]
	do Flags.set_level_flag("julian_refused_help", true)
	do Flags.add_game_counter("layla_closeness", 1)
	do actor_effect("Julian", "upright")
	do actor_change("Layla", "calm")
	do actor_change("Julian", "base")
	do actor_change("Fiona", "suspicious")
	Player: That's none of your business.
	do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
	Julian: Sure thing.
	Julian: Then my phone is none of yours.
	Julian: Good luck finding your dates.
	do actor_change("Julian", "base")
	do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
	Player: Yeah, well. Whatever.
	=> post_confrontation_discussion
- Tell him about Layla's deadline. [matters]
	do Flags.set_level_flag("julian_nearly_told_truth", true)
	do Flags.add_game_counter("layla_closeness", -1)
	do actor_effect("Julian", "upright")
	do actor_change("Julian", "base")
	do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
	Player: Fine. Layla has some sequencing—
	if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
		do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
		do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
		Layla: Fiona...!
		do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
	Julian: ...
	do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back_sad")
	Player: Hmm. Sorry, I forgot. We can't tell you.
	do actor_change("Julian", "talk")
	Julian: Right. Never mind, in that case.
	do actor_change("Julian", "annoyed_talk")
	Julian: Well, I'm afraid my kindness and my time run out here.
	Julian: All the best with... whatever it is you're trying to do.
	do actor_change("Julian", "base")
	do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
	Player: Yeah, well. Whatever.
	=> post_confrontation_discussion

~ post_confrontation_discussion
# julian walks off for good; from here it's fiona and layla alone (huddle layout).
do actor_change("Julian", "annoyed")
do actor_effect("Julian", "turn_away")
Julian turns back to his work without another word.
do SoundManager.fade_out_music(2.0)
do party_dismiss()
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	if Flags.get_level_flag("julian_nearly_told_truth") == true:
		do actor_change("Layla", "angry_talk")
		Layla: Fiona! You almost told him!
		do actor_change("Layla", "angry")
		do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back_sad")
		Player: I know. It slipped out. My bad.
		do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
		do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
		Layla: He's the last person who should know I haven't finished the sequencing...
		Layla: Or maybe, second last. I don't know...
		do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
		do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
		Player: Relax. He didn't get anything out of us.
		if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_work_reprimanded") == true:
			# step 2.296: the second hurt (the reprimand came first). layla is locked distant for the chapter.
			do Flags.lock_layla_distant()
			# step 2.375: the dimmed look is her sad eyes ("downcast", already set), held through the close-up
			do actor_focus("Layla", 1.6, 0.4)
			Somehow, you notice a change in Layla.
			The light behind her eyes seems dimmer. And she's looking at you differently.
			do actor_unfocus_all(0.3)
	else
		do actor_change("Layla", "talking")
		Layla: Well... that went great.
		do actor_change("Layla", "neutral")
		Player: Don't worry. He was never going to help us.
		do actor_change("Fiona", "shy")
		Player: I know him...
	do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
	Layla: So what now? My phone's dead, and yours...
	do actor_change("Layla", "attentive")
	do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
	Player: Can't get on the internet. Yes.
	do actor_change("Fiona", "thinking")
	Player: Hmm... I'm not sure.
	Player: All I know is that we need to find out that date one way or another.
	Player: The date DNA was discovered.
	if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
		do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
		Layla: ...Okay.
		do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
	else
		do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
		do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
		Layla: Got it. Let's do what we can!
		do actor_change("Layla", "eager")
	do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
	Player: Yep.
else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
do Flags.set_level_flag("dna_dates_lookup_pending", true)
=> END

~ leave
do actor_change("Julian", "base")
Julian: Mm.
do SoundManager.fade_out_music(2.0)
=> END
